say which localized key was asked for and by whom

CIDER_TRACE_LOCALIZED prints every key a bundle is asked for, what it answered, and the CALLER, from
__builtin_return_address. The caller is the point: a stripped application will not tell you which of
its call sites wanted a string, and a message send trace cannot help because it filters on the
receiver class, and NSBundle is the receiver for every one of them.

It settled a question that four rounds of static reading got WRONG. iA Writer shows Updating under
every filename in its library, and the disassembly appeared to say that the only reference to
Library_Snippet_Updating sat after a call to normalizedTextFromText:name: that a calibrated message
trace showed was never sent. One line closed it:

    CIDER_LOCALIZED Library_Snippet_Updating -> Updating... (from 0x100146563)

That return address belongs to the OTHER branch, the one taken when excerptProvider is nil. The
literal pool comment in the disassembly names the string at the naive lea target, and the code forms
its Swift String differently, so reading the comment instead of the running program pointed at the
wrong branch for four iterations.

--- a/src/NSBundle.m
+++ b/src/NSBundle.m
@@ -691,7 +691,18 @@
 
 - (NSString *)localizedStringForKey:(NSString *)key value:(NSString *)value table:(NSString *)tableName
 {
-    return [(NSString *)CFBundleCopyLocalizedString(_cfBundle, (CFStringRef)key, (CFStringRef)value, (CFStringRef)tableName) autorelease];
+    NSString *result = [(NSString *)CFBundleCopyLocalizedString(_cfBundle, (CFStringRef)key, (CFStringRef)value, (CFStringRef)tableName) autorelease];
+    const char *trace = getenv("CIDER_TRACE_LOCALIZED");
+
+    /* The return address names the caller, which is what a stripped application will not tell you. */
+    if (trace != NULL && trace[0] != '\0')
+    {
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_LOCALIZED %s -> %s (from %p)\n", [key UTF8String], [result UTF8String],
+                __builtin_return_address(0));
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
+
+    return result;
 }
 
 - (id)objectForInfoDictionaryKey:(NSString *)key
